OL,3,GNEWSAIllegal dump clear-up expected to
OL,4,Acost #240k
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe clear-up of more than 200 tonnes of
OL,7,Fillegally dumped waste is expected to
OL,8,Fcost about #238,000.
OL,10,FGloucester City Council was first made
OL,11,Faware of the site at Severnside Farm,
OL,12,Fnear St Oswald's Retail Park,
OL,13,FGloucester, in early 2026 and the land
OL,14,Fwas secured by the council, the
OL,15,FEnvironment Agency, and police.
OL,17,FBut, in July, the removal operation,
OL,18,Fwhich has so far cost #38,000, was
OL,19,Fhalted after asbestos was found.
OL,20,FCouncil leader Jeremy Hilton said the
OL,21,Fsafe disposal of what was left might
OL,22,Fcost an additional #200,000.
OL,23,APub: 02-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,348,340,200,160,0,100
